    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T20:05:06Z",
    "body": "Note from #1503 (M5): the confinement law is a shared helper on branch `mkinney:issue/1503-trochoid-confine`: `crates/app/src/operation/slot_fit.rs`, `pub(crate) fn refuse_unfit_slot(kind: &str, a: Point2, b: Point2, width: f64, region: &Region) -> Result<(), GenError>`. It refuses by name, with the numbers, a slot whose capsule (centre line A-B, half-width width/2) is not inside the given region; it takes the kind's label, so the Slot arm can call it unchanged. On that branch only the TrochoidalSlot arm of `operation/generate.rs` calls it (when the source is a selection). For Slot, the arm would first need the picked region: `Slot` is excluded in `material_region::selection_drives_region`, so it gets the authored stadium today, not the picks. Root cause, step-0 finding and repro are on #1503.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
