    "body": "fix on issue/1504-slot-selection · PR #1522 · pinned by slot_picks::{two_pocket_edges_give_a_slot_inside_the_pocket_and_undo_takes_it_back, the_floor_face_gives_the_slot_that_fits_it, a_slot_longer_than_the_picked_edges_is_refused_by_name_and_not_previewed, a_slot_wider_than_the_picked_edges_is_refused_by_name, a_slot_through_the_pocket_wall_is_refused_and_one_below_the_floor_holds_the_post, with_nothing_picked_the_typed_endpoints_rule_as_before, mcp_picks_seed_and_confine_the_slot_through_the_same_command}, machining2d::slot_room tests, ui slot_pick_page_tests (each mutation-checked) · merges when reviewed. Not stacked on #1513 (no shared hunks, merge-tree clean both ways); unifying the two confine laws is #1523. The page text now reads: a Slot is authored by its two endpoints and width, seeded from two picked opposite edges or a face and kept inside them.",
